Z||000014||thomas_l||10-03-2001||08:56 AM||||I believe that odor is common to GM cars built from 78 up to early 90's. Either the plastics or carpet, they all have it. I have worked on 100's of them and also owned an 80 Citation and 78 Bonneville. My 94 Bonneville also had it, just not as strong as the earlier models. <P>Now that I think about it, 1978 was the year GM really changed a lot of models. Again, in 1992-4, there was another total rehash of their line-up. Maybe those were the "stinky plastic" years  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||3
