Z||000021||mrfixit58||10-03-2001||02:32 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by My7Fieros:<BR><B>Yeah Ive noticed that to. But you know what car has it even more?...THE [b]VOLKSWAGEN BEETLE!</B> [/B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>I think the Beetle smell came from the from the seat padding. They used dryed moss (yes, the stuff in trees!). <P>I think the Smell in the Fiero can be traced to the seat foam or the carpet sound deadening. Although, when your clutch master cylindar decided to puke all it fluid onto you carpet it changes the smell..<BR><P>------------------<BR>Roy  :D <BR>Just another stock Blue 87 GT   <BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pennocksize.JPG">      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif"> ||||reg||1
